# Environment Variables Template for Google OAuth

# Add these to your .env file

# ======================
# Google OAuth Settings
# ======================

# Get these from Google Cloud Console:
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create/Select your project
# 3. Navigate to "APIs & Services" > "Credentials"
# 4. Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application)
# 5. Add authorized redirect URIs

# Your Google OAuth Client ID
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id-here.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Your Google OAuth Client Secret
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret-here

# The callback URL that Google will redirect to after authentication
# Development
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:3000/auth/google/callback

# Production (update this for your production domain)
# GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=https://your-production-domain.com/auth/google/callback

# ======================
# Google OAuth Setup Steps
# ======================

# 1. Create a Google Cloud Project:
#    - Visit https://console.cloud.google.com/
#    - Click "Select a project" > "New Project"
#    - Give your project a name (e.g., "KotobaMichi")
#    - Click "Create"

# 2. Enable Google+ API (if needed):
#    - In the left sidebar, go to "APIs & Services" > "Library"
#    - Search for "Google+ API"
#    - Click on it and press "Enable"

# 3. Create OAuth 2.0 Credentials:
#    - Go to "APIs & Services" > "Credentials"
#    - Click "Create Credentials" > "OAuth 2.0 Client ID"
#    - If prompted, configure the OAuth consent screen first:
#      * Choose "External" for user type (unless you have a workspace)
#      * Fill in the required fields:
#        - App name: KotobaMichi
#        - User support email: your-email@example.com
#        - Developer contact: your-email@example.com
#      * Add scopes: email, profile
#      * Save and continue
#    - Back to "Create OAuth Client ID":
#      * Application type: Web application
#      * Name: KotobaMichi Backend
#      * Authorized JavaScript origins:
#        - http://localhost:3000 (for development)
#        - https://your-production-domain.com (for production)
#      * Authorized redirect URIs:
#        - http://localhost:3000/auth/google/callback (for development)
#        - https://your-production-domain.com/auth/google/callback (for production)
#      * Click "Create"

# 4. Copy Credentials:
#    - After creation, you'll see a dialog with your Client ID and Client Secret
#    - Copy the Client ID and paste it into GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID above
#    - Copy the Client Secret and paste it into GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET above

# 5. Important Notes:
#    - Keep your Client Secret secure and never commit it to version control
#    - For production, use HTTPS for all redirect URIs
#    - Update the OAuth consent screen with your privacy policy and terms of service URLs
#    - Test thoroughly in development before deploying to production

# ======================
# Testing Your Setup
# ======================

# After setting up the environment variables:
# 1. Restart your backend server: pnpm start:dev
# 2. Visit: http://localhost:3000/auth/google
# 3. You should be redirected to Google's sign-in page
# 4. After signing in, you should be redirected back with tokens

# ======================
# Troubleshooting
# ======================

# Error: "redirect_uri_mismatch"
# - Ensure your GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL exactly matches one of the redirect URIs in Google Console
# - Check for trailing slashes and protocol (http vs https)

# Error: "Access blocked: This app's request is invalid"
# - Your OAuth consent screen might not be configured properly
# - Make sure you've added the required scopes (email, profile)
# - Verify your app is not in "Testing" mode with no test users added

# Error: "invalid_client"
# - Check that your GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET are correct
# - Ensure there are no extra spaces or characters

# ======================
# Production Checklist
# ======================

# Before deploying to production:
# ☐ Update GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL to use your production domain
# ☐ Add production domain to authorized JavaScript origins in Google Console
# ☐ Add production callback URL to authorized redirect URIs in Google Console
# ☐ Ensure HTTPS is enabled on your production server
# ☐ Set COOKIE_SECURE=true in production
# ☐ Configure OAuth consent screen with privacy policy and terms of service
# ☐ Consider moving OAuth consent screen from "Testing" to "Production" status
# ☐ Test the OAuth flow on production
